 "drivingQuestion": "What is a totefet?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Totefet is identified as a forehead ornament, supported by a baraita",
 "continuesQuestionOf": "shabbat.sugya286",
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.57b.10",
   "daf": "57b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "אֲמַר לֵיהּ אַבָּיֵי: תִּהְוֵי כְּקָמֵיעַ מוּמְחֶה, וְתִשְׁתְּרֵי!",
   "en": "«Abaye said to him: And let» the legal status of «this» packet «be like» that of «an effective amulet,» whose effectiveness is proven, «and» it should «be permitted,» as an effective amulet may be moved on Shabbat."
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.57b.11",
   "daf": "57b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "אֶלָּא אָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה מִשְּׁמֵיהּ דְּאַבָּיֵי: אֲפוּזְיָינֵי. תַּנְיָא נָמֵי הָכִי: יוֹצְאָה אִשָּׁה בִּסְבָכָה הַמּוּזְהֶבֶת, וּבְטוֹטֶפֶת וּבְסַרְבִּיטִין הַקְּבוּעִין בָּהּ.",
   "en": "«Rather, Rav Yehuda said in the name of Abaye:» A totefet is an «appuzainu,» an ornament worn on the forehead. This opinion «was also taught» in a baraita: «A woman may go out with a gilded hairnet» worn to hold the hair in place, «and with the totefet, and with the sarvitin that are fastened to the hairnet,» since a woman would not remove her head covering to show her friend those ornaments."
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.57b.12",
   "daf": "57b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "אֵיזוֹ טוֹטֶפֶת וְאֵיזוֹ סַרְבִּיטִין? אָמַר רַבִּי אֲבָהוּ: טוֹטֶפֶת — הַמּוּקֶּפֶת לָהּ מֵאֹזֶן לְאֹזֶן. סַרְבִּיטִין — הַמַּגִּיעִין לָהּ עַד לְחָיֶיהָ.",
   "en": "And they said: «Which is a totefet and which is sarvitin? Rabbi Abbahu said: Totefet is that which goes around her» forehead «from ear to ear. Sarvitin are those» attached to the net «that reach» down «to her cheeks.»"
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.57b.13",
   "daf": "57b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "אָמַר רַב הוּנָא: עֲנִיּוֹת עוֹשִׂין אוֹתָן שֶׁל מִינֵי צִבְעוֹנִין, עֲשִׁירוֹת עוֹשִׂין אוֹתָן שֶׁל כֶּסֶף וְשֶׁל זָהָב.",
   "en": "«Rav Huna said: Poor women make» these ornaments «from» different «types of colored» materials. «Wealthy women make them of silver and of gold.»"
  }
 ],
